/-!
# One coordinate enlargement with projective quotient

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 05A9, `theorem-ffdescent-projectivity`,
successor paragraph (blueprint: lem-trf-coordinate-projective-successor).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v w t s

open scoped TensorProduct DirectSum

namespace Submodule

/-- Enlarge a scalar-extension coordinate submodule to contain a specified element,
with countably generated projective quotient. The quotient inclusion is the map induced
by `V.subtype`. The isomorphism `ρ` is characterized on pure tensors and every remaining
coordinate, so it is precisely the quotient identification induced by `θ` and projection.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 05A9, `theorem-ffdescent-projectivity`,
successor paragraph (blueprint: lem-trf-coordinate-projective-successor).

Proof:
1. Put `L = M/U`. Tensor right exactness (`lem-weil-pbc-tensor-right-exact`) identifies
   the kernel of the tensor quotient map with the tensor image of `U`. The hypothesis
   identifies this with the `H`-coordinate submodule. Projection onto the remaining
   coordinates has that same kernel and is surjective by extension by zero. These two
   quotient maps induce `ρ`, with the pure-tensor coordinate formula stated below.
2. Apply `lem-trf-countable-submodule-adapted-to-base-change-sum` to the cyclic submodule
   generated by the image of `x` in `L`. It gives a countably generated submodule `P`
   containing that image whose tensor image is the `J`-coordinate submodule of the
   remaining direct sum. This step needs no flatness or projectivity.
3. Flatness preserves `P ↪ L` (`lem-trf-flat-tensor-preserves-injection`). Its tensor
   image is therefore isomorphic to the direct sum over `J`. This sum is projective
   (`lem-weil-pbc-projective-direct-sum-family`), and projectivity transfers through
   the isomorphism (`lem-weil-pbc-projective-direct-summand`). The pure tensors of a
   countable spanning subset of `P` span its scalar extension. Apply
   `lem-trf-countable-projective-faithfully-flat-descent` to conclude that `P` is
   countably generated and projective over `A`.
4. Take `V` to be the inverse image of `P` under `M → L`. Then `U ≤ V` and `x ∈ V`.
   The restriction `V → P` is surjective with kernel `U`, so `V/U ≃ₗ[A] P` by sending
   the class of `v` to its image in `L`. This transfers countable generation and
   projectivity to `V/U`.
5. The tensor image of `V` contains the `H`-coordinate submodule. Tensor right
   exactness for `V → P` says that its projection to the remaining coordinates is the
   `J`-coordinate submodule. A submodule containing a projection's kernel is the
   inverse image of its projected image. This proves the `H ∪ J` coordinate identity.
6. The canonical `V/U → M/U` is the preceding isomorphism followed by `P ↪ L`.
   Flat tensoring makes it injective. Tensoring that isomorphism identifies its image
   with the image of the tensor inclusion of `P`, which `ρ` identifies with the
   `J`-coordinate submodule. The formula in step 1 fixes the required identification.
-/
theorem exists_coordinate_projective_successor
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {B : Type v} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [Module.FaithfullyFlat A B] {M : Type w} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]
    {I : Type t} {Q : I → Type s} [∀ i, AddCommGroup (Q i)] [∀ i, Module B (Q i)]
    (hQcount : ∀ i, ∃ c : Set (Q i), c.Countable ∧ Submodule.span B c = ⊤)
    (hQproj : ∀ i, Module.Projective B (Q i))
    (θ : B ⊗[A] M ≃ₗ[B] ⨁ i : I, Q i) (U : Submodule A M) (H : Set I)
    (hU : LinearMap.range (θ.toLinearMap.comp (U.subtype.baseChange B)) =
      DirectSum.coordinateSubmodule B I Q H) (x : M) (hx : x ∉ U) :
    ∃ (V : Submodule A M) (J : Set I),
      J ⊆ Hᶜ ∧ U ≤ V ∧ x ∈ V ∧
      LinearMap.range (θ.toLinearMap.comp (V.subtype.baseChange B)) =
        DirectSum.coordinateSubmodule B I Q (H ∪ J) ∧
      (∃ c : Set (V ⧸ U.comap V.subtype),
        c.Countable ∧ Submodule.span A c = ⊤) ∧
      Module.Projective A (V ⧸ U.comap V.subtype) ∧
      Function.Injective
        (((U.comap V.subtype).mapQ U V.subtype le_rfl).baseChange B) ∧
      ∃ ρ : B ⊗[A] (M ⧸ U) ≃ₗ[B] ⨁ i : {i : I // i ∉ H}, Q i.val,
        (∀ (b : B) (m : M) (i : {i : I // i ∉ H}),
          ρ (b ⊗ₜ[A] U.mkQ m) i = θ (b ⊗ₜ[A] m) i.val) ∧
        LinearMap.range (ρ.toLinearMap.comp
          (((U.comap V.subtype).mapQ U V.subtype le_rfl).baseChange B)) =
          DirectSum.coordinateSubmodule B {i : I // i ∉ H} (fun i : {i : I // i ∉ H} ↦ Q i.val)
            {i : {i : I // i ∉ H} | i.val ∈ J} := by
  sorry

end Submodule
